<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>The week in pictures: Protests across France, wildfires in Indonesia and Brazilian elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e29d3d9d2a1fbf14872d79f3682e30db780078cd32c7de5314bd2865bbae94b</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:48:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections--3fb12d327891.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">From student protests across France over the weekend and presidential elections in Brazil pitting leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro to wildfires in Indonesia, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Voting under way across Brazil in tight presidential run-off between Lula and Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7db069e6b45bd5105e782a282adb9b72b600a46b03346e427ec24664638a5ec8</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:46:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonar--05fa1f528dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s 158 million voters decide between leftist President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and right-wing challenger Senator Flavio Bolsonaro – the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro – following a highly charged run-off campaign period, with the candidates in a dead heat in polls. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Brazil presidential runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bb1bb9c80b2776710eea8a3478f8462e8868980b7abe7d89f1ed2a9b1306cfb</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:40:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff--8d55229e95d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption. France 24 Jan Onoszko telles us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Far-right leader Le Pen says visible policing keeps protests smooth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:500ce6200226b3920c51258d4cf84ff222f52a72ee88e61ad502ac8c89674c9e</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:39:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/far-right-leader-le-pen-says-visible-policing-keeps-protests-smooth--be7e44d78d09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/far-right-leader-le-pen-says-visible-policing-keeps-protests-smooth" /><summary type="html">Meanwhile, France’s far-right National Rally is holding the second day of its party congress in Orléans, south of Paris. Marine Le Pen is expected to officially launch her presidential campaign in a speech later this afternoon, while Jordan Bardella is being re-elected as party leader. On Saturday, a large counter-demonstration against the far right was held in the city. Our reporter Antonia Kerrigan has been following the latest developments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:236a50790d95387a6e0a88976a92a0961564a9a37654dc2a8aedf3ca6e5a67ae</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election--605d00c22edc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>Obama hits campaign trail for democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:980ec20c47e9fc0409e10e5145c9f469d41483b55034717e1d3f7668fc213edc</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:36:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats--dc300583e461.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">With less than two weeks to go before the US midterm elections, former President Barack Obama has hit the campaign trail, rallying support for Democratic candidates in the key states of Michigan and Ohio. He criticised the Trump administration, blaming the White House for rising living costs, a major concern for voters. Democrats are hoping to regain control of Congress, with polls showing several closely contested races. Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bb36c5c979b8b025c741b9c30548d2300e8dcc53fc2fbb4d90d578f84f3dd60</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron--c0b8d6b2a6c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron" /><summary type="html">More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 1,300 people arrested in mass weekend protests across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50b1670d29b8a12ac6c2f217f2bd7e647a1a3a213250d2fc0d6d4d2c0045575c</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:02:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-at-least-1-300-people-arrested-in-mass-weekend-protests-across-france--e24f12ed1515.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-at-least-1-300-people-arrested-in-mass-weekend-protests-across-france" /><summary type="html">At least 1,300 people were arrested on the sidelines of Saturday's protests across France and at least 50 officers and three protesters were hurt, the interior ministry said Sunday. The arrests occurred as clashes broke out on the margins of largely calm demonstrations in major cities over the high cost of living.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Suspect in racist gun attack near Paris transferred to psychiatric unit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69026add8ac76b7fe23c9ce13ffb4ddf73fbe8a573c9bb4077156a3cd732b90c</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T10:36:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-suspect-in-racist-gun-attack-near-paris-transferred-to-psychiatric-unit--4ab912be23c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-suspect-in-racist-gun-attack-near-paris-transferred-to-psychiatric-unit" /><summary type="html">A shooter suspected of killing one person and wounding five others on Friday in the town of Trappes, near Paris, has had his police custody suspended for a 48-hour psychiatric observation, anti-terror prosecutors said Sunday. The 39-year-old man is believed to have had racist motivations behind the gun attack as most of the victims had foreign origins.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Some clashes erupted at end of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecabf3beb093b0220e81b30bf394d4a3cd48b1afc8b850f89359d7f1a1a8269e</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:35:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-some-clashes-erupted-at-end-of-protests--0c66a7dc9b2a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-some-clashes-erupted-at-end-of-protests" /><summary type="html">There were some clashes on Saturday, mainly in major cities and as demonstrations came to an end. French authorities say police made nearly 1,000 arrests nationwide. Here’s a report from our sister channel, France 2.</summary></entry><entry><title>More than 400.000 protest across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69122fa2ae1bd05e83dc2958ff3bbabd863fffe16af89d594f7aa524e20f1367</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:32:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/more-than-400-000-protest-across-france--ddecf64571e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-400-000-protest-across-france" /><summary type="html">Saturday’s demonstrations across France were largely peaceful, easing fears of a repeat of the violence seen last weekend. Hundreds of thousands took to the streets to demand action on the rising cost of living and more funding for public services, with students, workers and retirees marching side by side. Many say their anger shows no sign of fading. The government put turnout at 410,000 nationwide, while the CGT union estimated the figure was almost twice as high. Here’s Jack Pownall with more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s far right gathers as Le Pen prepares her presidential campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dce4e85c7212ea93afdfd397dac1878c57bf4d214a6857e29bea213125e0dde</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:31:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-gathers-as-le-pen-prepares-her-presidential-campaign--73e7ad8469e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-gathers-as-le-pen-prepares-her-presidential-campaign" /><summary type="html">Meanwhile, France’s far-right National Rally is holding the second day of its party congress in Orléans, south of Paris. Marine Le Pen is expected to officially launch her presidential campaign in a speech later this afternoon, while Jordan Bardella is being re-elected as party leader. On Saturday, a large counter-demonstration against the far right was held in the city. For more on what’s happening there, let’s cross to our reporter, Antonia Kerrigan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of thousands march in France to protest against government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68a8094777b4ec5e9633caf2c0199df9c38989fbeca4d64ffb434b0209827b6a</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:29:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hundreds-of-thousands-march-in-france-to-protest-against-government--bc9fb991d30d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-of-thousands-march-in-france-to-protest-against-government" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands marched across France on Saturday protesting the rising cost of living and a lack of government resources for essential services like schools. While demonstrations in Paris started peacefully they ended with a heavy security response, with almost 1,000 arrested across the country. France 24 International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia holds parliamentary election as populist leader Vucic faces student movement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:182ce4835b4d6be2a4c465b2e27f1b950afaacae1b4841cd4959cc50ff402e59</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:14:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement--d43323a472f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement" /><summary type="html">Serbia votes on Sunday in what is set to be its most contested parliamentary election in more than 14 years, as a student-led movement seeks to oust the party of populist leader Aleksandar Vucic. The vote comes after nearly two years of student-led protests sparked by the 2024 collapse of a canopy that killed 16 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to know as Brazilians choose between Lula and Bolsonaro in tense presidential runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66de7e3cef65d5c03465fac902e3a5bf7b5177076542cff19815430b9a7afa4f</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T06:05:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff--2a6bd58b70ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilians are set on Sunday to choose between leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro in the runoff vote of a deeply polarizing presidential election, and one which will determine whether the US significantly expands its growing influence in Latin America.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Government says protests across France 'went well' despite nearly 1,000 arrests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcc04fdecfb18b5e69ea793470e52ae629f3671be085bd0827f1bd1f21ec62b9</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T21:01:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-the-marches-went-well-_-french-government-on-demonstrations-a-week-after-looting-and-violen--49f1f5595d28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261024-the-marches-went-well-%E2%80%93-french-government-on-demonstrations-a-week-after-looting-and-violence" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands marched across France on Saturday protesting the rising cost of living and a lack of government resources for essential services like schools. While demonstrations in Paris started peacefully they ended with a heavy security response, with almost 1,000 arrested across the country.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Watching the Post-Riot Protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b49ec496d5bb4401036a32ca986ece6bd0ea0272263f16aee0e2cca9d4b57ac3</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-france-watching-the-post-riot-protests--92360a9de2c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-france-watching-the-post-riot-protests" /><summary type="html">After the French protests turned into riots last weekend, the curfews, and then the alleged racist mass shooting yesterday on the outskirts of Paris, there has been much anxiety, planning and preparation ahead of today's protests.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>“Witkoff should step down” says Ukraine Committee Chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:332d4e34d33577c1cff25b56adbe77b82ef293333b1a0974d47aa42e6e09029d</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-witkoff-should-step-down-says-ukraine-committee-chief--c1a0869eb9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261024-witkoff-should-step-down-says-ukraine-committee-chief" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s access to Starlink and Starshield satellite links has been restored to the speeds it had before restrictions that disrupted front-line operations for more than a week, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Saturday.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands take to Tel Aviv's streets for protests against Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fde8a543efef0262321c7f576dff7284293da8926a84537b7dc5db1b5f51d24a</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu--99da939090a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched against Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government in Tel Aviv on Saturday – just three days before Israel's general election – demanding accountability for the failure to prevent a Hamas-led attack on October 7, 2023, which led to the war in Gaza.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthi rebels claim new attacks on oil facilities and airports across Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ae842fc17b73834914667fe29c68fcd35798c25bde2eb488f408f9a37ddcde4</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:50:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia--98ea10f02978.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-allied Houthi rebels said they launched attacks at Saudi oil facilities and airports on Saturday while Yemen’s Saudi-backed government ​said the ‌group also fired three ballistic missiles at coast guard sites in ⁠the port city of Aden.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>France: Clashes erupt as protests sweep across cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdf1914d43cfde0733139c317448fb04aaf57d8fe2f42244c87056a1d6a4069d</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:50:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261024-france-clashes-erupt-as-protests-sweep-across-cities--f4d537999c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261024-france-clashes-erupt-as-protests-sweep-across-cities" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 The Ministry of the Interior estimates at least 410,000 people rallied across France for Saturday’s protests against the high cost of living, including 110,000 in Paris. 
 
Meanwhile, reported nearly 800,000 demonstrators and 250,000 in the capital. 
 
The situation in Paris remained largely "calm" during the day, while clashes broke out in other cities following attempts to enter unauthorised areas.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel begins demolitions in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c72bdaa74dd274d7f6ee71a803c06358b8e72ac90f3e7b6543bbfa8a2c0f0f58</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:13:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank--1cdd8864f331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">The Palestinian Authority has called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. The head of Hebron's municipality said an additional 1,300 may also be forced to leave.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy hit by new cost of living protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c9553d3af97927bc0f72d19b3ebdf21a21bef833300dec826ee01261ee910f8</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:12:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/italy-hit-by-new-cost-of-living-protests--26c6e84f6720.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/italy-hit-by-new-cost-of-living-protests" /><summary type="html">Soldiers were deployed across Milan and luxury boutiques boarded up as protesters took to the streets again on Saturday, a week after looting and clashes with police. Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni announced a series of measures, including sending an additional 500 soldiers to the city and introducing tougher penalties for minors, who police said made up a large proportion of last week’s violent protesters. Surveillance helicopters circled central Piazza del Duomo, while soldiers patrolled in groups alongside military vehicles and a water cannon. Some visitors said they would leave the city centre if violence broke out again. Our Rome correspondent, Seema Gupta, has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris: 70.000 police officers deployed nationwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bb91ccb0a525c14fed42c207b87c6a4021251720eb64c732cf672b9e65bf708</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:17:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:11:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-70-000-police-officers-deployed-nationwide--5be209d838b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-70-000-police-officers-deployed-nationwide" /><summary type="html">A coalition of the “Yellow Vests” movement, trade unions and students will march across France on Saturday with demands over studying conditions and purchasing power. Some 70,000 police are expected to be deployed as authorities fear looting and vandalism similar to last Saturday's unrest. Jennie Shin speaks to France 24's reporter Elitsa Gadeva.</summary></entry></feed>
